# openOODA v2: Comprehensive Zero-Trust Capability Model

**Location:** `openOODA/CAPS.oot`  
**Scope:** V2 capability catalog for product and `std/src/ooda/`  
**Purpose:** Single list agents must read when gating code. Mirrors `DESIGN.oot` §3.1 + V2 Architecture. Status lives in `PM.oot` §3.

**In plain English:** Before, one network token gave full access. Now we split it into small tokens. You give only what the code needs from `main()`. Each token is checked when you compile. At run time the process re-checks a process-local seal before the effect runs; forged or missing tokens fail closed. **[STATUS: path-A process-local token re-check. CAP-G1 net op→preferred granular map is path-A (Http/Tcp/Udp/Bind + NetCap supersede). CAP-G2 fs op→preferred granular map is path-A (FsRead/FsWrite + FsCap supersede; keep `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` write overlay). Full `seccomp-bpf` / `SIGSYS` OS isolation, unforgeable object-caps, sys/process granular (CAP-G4), and unused V2 grants (CAP-G3) are residual — do **not** claim full OS isolation. 8-byte token randomness residual; see DESIGN §3.1]**

The core principle is **least privilege at the compiler**. Every capability is checked at compile time and enforced at run time.

Here is the master list of `&Cap` tokens in the V2 ecosystem. **Count note:** `DESIGN.oot` §V2 Architecture counts **18** new granular tokens that fractured `SysCap`/`NetCap`. The list below shows **27** entries because it keeps the 2 legacy broad tokens for compat plus 7 related tokens (`EnvCap`, `MemCap`, `FfiCap`, etc.) that DESIGN groups under §3. **`is_cap_type` accepts all 27.** Use granular tokens for **new** `std/` and product code.

### Path-A honesty (do not greenwash)

| Layer | What is true today |
|-------|--------------------|
| **Type accept** | All 27 names below are valid `&Cap` types in check (`oodac/check_cap_util.oo`). |
| **Sealed ops (net / CAP-G1)** | **path-A:** `sealed_net_kind_of` returns preferred Http/Tcp/Udp/Bind/NetCap; check accepts exact preferred **or** legacy NetCap; wrong granular denied (HttpCap↛`tcp_bind`). Smoke: `cap_g1_net_granular_smoke.sh`. |
| **Sealed ops (fs / CAP-G2)** | **path-A:** `sealed_fs_kind_of` returns preferred FsReadCap/FsWriteCap; check accepts exact preferred **or** legacy FsCap supersede; wrong granular denied (FsWriteCap↛`read_file`; FsReadCap↛`write_file`). Helpers: `cap_fs_granted_ok` / `cap_fs_argflow_ok`. |
| **Sealed ops (other non-net)** | Still **legacy** kinds: `SysCap`, `EnvCap`, plus `TimeCap` / `RandCap` / `AllocCap` / `UnsafeFFICap` / `ThreadCap` / `GpuCap`. Process/Sync/Mem/HW/UI sealed enforce residual (**CAP-G3/G4+**). |
| **Runtime require (net)** | **path-A:** `oo_cap_require_{http,tcp,udp,bind}` accept granular **or** `g_tok_net`; `sock_raw` NetCap-only. **Not** OS seccomp isolation of sockets. |
| **Runtime require (fs)** | **path-A:** `oo_cap_require_fsread` / `oo_cap_require_fswrite` accept granular **or** `g_tok_fs` (FsCap supersede). Wrong granular fails closed. Write still gated by **`OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`** policy overlay. **Not** OS path sandbox / landlock / full FS isolation. |
| **Runtime grants** | Header declares many `oo_cap_grant_*` (incl. granular). Emit injects legacy set + partial granular (`tcp` / `fsread` / `process` today); full main-param grant matrix for every V2 name residual (**CAP-G3**). |
| **Policy overlays (not Cap types)** | `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` on writes; `sys_exec` child env filter (`OODA_`/`OO_` + minimal PATH); FFI nested-`dlopen` refuse — see residual links. |
| **Not a Cap** | `// SECRET:` taint / sink refuse is **IFC**, not a capability token. Do not add SECRET to this list. |
| **Isolation ceiling** | Process-local tokens + check refuse. **Do not claim** full OS isolation, complete `seccomp-bpf`/`SIGSYS` coverage, or unforgeable object-caps across hostile rewrite. |

### CAP-G1 path-A map (net)

**Legacy supersede:** `&NetCap` may satisfy soft-granular preferred ops (one-wave compat). **Hard NetCap-only:** `sock_raw` / `raw_socket`.

| Preferred cap | Sealed ops (product or residual emit) | Runtime require (target) |
|---------------|----------------------------------------|--------------------------|
| **`&HttpCap`** | `fetch`; residual names `http_get` / `net_get` / `net_connect` / `downloadData` / `query_remote_api` | `oo_cap_require_http` (or NetCap) |
| **`&TcpCap`** | `tcp_connect` / `tcp_write` / `tcp_read` / `tcp_close` / `tls_connect` | `oo_cap_require_tcp` (or NetCap) |
| **`&BindCap`** | `tcp_bind` | `oo_cap_require_bind` (or NetCap) |
| **`&UdpCap`** | `bind_udp` / `udp_recv` | `oo_cap_require_udp` (or NetCap) |
| **`&NetCap`** (only) | `sock_raw` / `raw_socket` | `oo_cap_require_net` — always Err residual product |

**New code:** prefer the granular token that matches the op. **Compat:** keep `&NetCap` until call sites migrate (std majority still legacy — CAP-G6).

### CAP-G2 path-A map (fs)

**Legacy supersede:** `&FsCap` may satisfy soft-granular preferred fs ops (one-wave compat). **No hard FsCap-only product op** (unlike net `sock_raw`); broad `FsCap` is supersede-only for soft read/write. **Wrong granular fail-closed:** `FsReadCap` must **not** authorize write; `FsWriteCap` must **not** authorize read/path/size.

| Preferred cap | Sealed ops (product or residual emit) | Runtime require (target) |
|---------------|----------------------------------------|--------------------------|
| **`&FsReadCap`** | `read_file` / `fs_read` / `path_exists` / `file_size` | `oo_cap_require_fsread` (or FsCap) |
| **`&FsWriteCap`** | `write_file` / `fs_write` | `oo_cap_require_fswrite` (or FsCap) + **`OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`** overlay |

**New code:** prefer `&FsReadCap` for read/probe/size, `&FsWriteCap` for create/modify. **Compat:** keep `&FsCap` until call sites migrate (`std/os/fs.oo` still legacy — CAP-G6). **Not claimed:** OS FS isolation, landlock, or complete `seccomp-bpf` on open/write (CAP-G5 residual honesty).

### 1. File System & Memory
* **`&FsCap`**: Broad filesystem access **(legacy — supersedes soft-granular FsReadCap/FsWriteCap for one-wave compat). Prefer granular below for new APIs.**
* **`&FsReadCap`**: Preferred for read/probe sealed ops (`read_file` / `fs_read` / `path_exists` / `file_size`). **Must not** authorize write alone once CAP-G2 check map is path-A.
* **`&FsWriteCap`**: Preferred for create/modify sealed ops (`write_file` / `fs_write`). **Must not** authorize read/path/size alone. Writes still fail-closed under `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` (policy overlay, not a Cap type).
* **`&AllocCap`**: Permission to allocate heap memory (`malloc`/`free`).
* **`&MemCap`**: Permission to use shared memory or `mmap` across boundaries.

### 2. Network & Web
* **`&NetCap`**: Broad network access **(legacy — supersedes soft-granular Http/Tcp/Udp/Bind for one-wave compat; required for `sock_raw` / `raw_socket`). Prefer granular below for new APIs.**
* **`&HttpCap`**: Preferred for HTTP-ish sealed ops (`fetch` product; other names residual emit). **Must not** authorize raw bind/connect alone.
* **`&TcpCap`**: Preferred for client TCP slot IO + `tls_connect` (TLS product only when OpenSSL linked).
* **`&UdpCap`**: Preferred for UDP bind/recv.
* **`&BindCap`**: Preferred for TCP listen/bind (`tcp_bind`).

### 3. OS & Execution
* **`&SysCap`**: Broad OS execution **(legacy — prefer granular below; kept for compat).**
* **`&ProcessCap`**: Spawn subprocesses (`fork`/`exec`) only.
* **`&SyncCap`**: Use IPC, Mutexes, and Semaphores only.
* **`&ThreadCap`**: Spawn parallel CPU threads.
* **`&EnvCap`**: Read environment variables.

### 4. Hardware & Peripherals
* **`&GpuCap`**: Run parallel work on the GPU/NPU.
* **`&UsbCap`**: Direct hardware passthrough (for I2C).
* **`&AudioCap`**: Read mic / write speakers.
* **`&CameraCap`**: Read raw video frames from a webcam.
* **`&HidCap`**: Read keyboard/mouse events (checks keyloggers).

### 5. UI & Display
* **`&WindowCap`**: Request a GUI window from the OS compositor.
* **`&FrameCap`**: Map pixels directly to the framebuffer (for hologram engines).

### 6. Audit & Security
* **`&AuditCap`**: Write to the append-only, cryptographic audit trail.
* **`&SignCap`**: Use the host Secure Enclave (TPM/HSM) to sign payloads.
* **`&HitlCap`** (Human-In-The-Loop): Freeze the thread and prompt the human for YubiKey or biometric.
* **`&TimeCap`**: Read the system clock. Without it, you cannot measure time (helps limit timing side channels).
* **`&RandCap`**: Read from `/dev/urandom` (cryptographically secure random).
* **`&FfiCap`** (`&UnsafeFFICap` alias): Run unsafe C bindings. Most dangerous. Requires explicit grant.

