**When to read this file:** When you add or gate code that touches files, network, OS, hardware, UI, or security — and always when you edit `std/src/ooda/` (see `BOOTSTRAP.oot` tier *Security, sandboxing, capability gating* + `DESIGN.oot` §3).

*Update this list when a token is added or fractured. Keep count note in sync with DESIGN. Prefer granular tokens in new APIs. CAP-G1/G2 preferred maps are path-A process-local seal contracts; do **not** claim full OS isolation, complete `seccomp-bpf`/`SIGSYS`, or that CAP-G3+ families are done.*
